When `--check-paths` is enabled, checking the existence of `run.model_id_or_path` directly via `Path::new(&run.model_id_or_path).exists()` will always fail if the path starts with an environment variable (e.g., `$MODELS_DIR/model.gguf`), because the path is not resolved first. This leads to false-positive "model path not found" errors even when the environment variable is correctly set and the resolved path exists.

We should resolve the environment variable first, and then perform the existence check on the resolved path.

